<!--
  The suction grip, for any scene that has the tool (models/tool.xml) in it.
  Include it once at the top level of the scene, next to the other parts:

    <include file="suction.xml"/>

  It cannot live in tool.xml, which is included inside a body, where MuJoCo
  does not allow an <equality> section.

  MuJoCo has no suction cup. The stand-in is one weld constraint between the
  tool and a module. It starts switched off and with no module: its second
  body is the world, which never matters while it is off. Suction::Grip
  (src/suction.h) writes the module's id and the relative pose the two have
  at that moment into the model's copy of this weld and switches it on;
  Suction::Release switches it off. One weld serves every module, so the
  pallet needs nothing for it.

  solref and solimp set how stiff the weld is: a time constant of 5 ms and
  an impedance of 0.99 at any stretch. Measured by tests/suction_test.cc, a
  30 kg module held still sags by 0.004 mm and turns by less than 0.001
  degrees, standing or flat, and does not creep; during a brisk carry
  (7.5 m/s^2) it strays at most 0.07 mm and 0.02 degrees and comes back.
  MuJoCo raises the time constant to twice the timestep if the timestep is
  ever made larger than 2.5 ms.

  torquescale weighs turning against sliding. It is a length: think of it as
  the size of the patch of glue that the weld stands for. 1 m is about the
  size of the cup pattern.
-->
<mujocoinclude>
  <equality>
    <weld name="suction" body1="tool" active="false" torquescale="1"
          solref="0.005 1" solimp="0.99 0.99 0.001 0.5 2"/>
  </equality>
</mujocoinclude>
